# ============================================================================
# Nobridge CRM ops workspace — root .gitignore
# This repo (VAV-TECH-2/nobridge-crm-ops) is PUBLIC. Anything secret, PII,
# oversized, or belonging to a nested repo is excluded here.
# ============================================================================

# --- Nested git repos (each has its own GitHub remote; never track here) ----
# twenty/            -> VAV-TECH-2/CRM (frontend fork, canonical remote "vt2")
# .crm-automations/dashboard/ -> VAV-TECH-2/nobridge-ops-dashboard
/twenty/
/.crm-automations/dashboard/

# --- SECRETS (delivered to teammates via the secrets bundle, never git) -----
# Live long-lived Twenty API JWT:
/.crm-sales-engine/engine_twenty_token.txt
# Live long-lived Twenty API JWT for the website sign-up integration:
/.crm-sales-engine/website_twenty_token.txt
# Scripts with hardcoded OAuth client secret / refresh tokens:
/.crm-sales-engine/test_e2e.py
/.crm-sales-engine/test_reconcile.py
/.crm-sales-engine/oauth_exchange.py
# Retired-agent backups containing plaintext old credentials:
/_archive/
# The generated secrets bundle + password file (belt-and-braces; they're written outside the repo):
nobridge-crm-secrets-*.zip
nobridge-crm-secrets-PASSWORD*

# --- Prospect data / PII / operational state (public repo => keep local) ----
/.crm-fulfillment/created.json
/.crm-fulfillment/state.json
/.crm-fulfillment/networking_meta.json
/.crm-fulfillment/networking_moved.json
/.crm-fulfillment/rollback_*.json
/.crm-migrate/resolved.json
/.crm-migrate/dump.txt
/.crm-migrate/lastcontact.txt
/.crm-migrate/lastcontact.sql
/.crm-migrate-seller/resolved.json
/.crm-migrate-seller/dump.txt
/.crm-migrate-seller/lastcontact.txt
/.crm-migrate-seller/lastcontact.sql
/.crm-sales-engine/stage_migration_manifest.json
# v2 migration rollback state — same class as the stage_migration_manifest above. The scripts are
# worth sharing; what they did to this one workspace (449 record ids and their previous stages) is
# local operational state. NOTE: these files are the ONLY way to reverse 01-04 and 07 — they are
# gitignored, not disposable. Do not clear .crm-migrate-v2/manifests/ to "tidy up".
/.crm-migrate-v2/manifests/
/.crm-migrate-v2/VERIFIED
*.log
*.xlsx
*.csv

# --- pipeline-autopilot local state ----------------------------------------
# THIS REPO IS PUBLIC. autopilot.db is the audit trail, and its `decisions.evidence_json` holds the
# subjects and bodies of real client email plus the model's reasoning about named companies. That is
# PII and it must never be committed. The scripts are worth sharing; what this one workspace's deals
# said to each other is not. Same reasoning as the migration manifests above: gitignored, NOT
# disposable — autopilot.db is the only record of what was changed and the only way to revert it.
/.crm-automations/pipeline-autopilot/data/
/.crm-automations/pipeline-autopilot/*.db
/.crm-automations/pipeline-autopilot/*.db-wal
/.crm-automations/pipeline-autopilot/*.db-shm

# --- ai-access local state --------------------------------------------------
# aiaccess.db holds TOKEN HASHES and the request log, and the request log stores the arguments each
# tool was called with — which will contain fragments of client email as soon as anybody pastes one
# into a chat. Same rule as autopilot.db: gitignored, not disposable. It is also the only record of
# who asked the CRM what. The deal writes an AI made are NOT here; they are in autopilot.db, so that
# one revert tool undoes both.
/.crm-automations/ai-access/data/
/.crm-automations/ai-access/*.db
/.crm-automations/ai-access/*.db-wal
/.crm-automations/ai-access/*.db-shm
/.crm-automations/ai-access/ai-access.env

# --- Oversized / stale artifacts (GitHub hard limit is 100 MB per file) -----
/.deploy-tmp/
/deploy/finance/_artifact/

# --- OS / editor / language junk -------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.venv/
node_modules/
